<title>SINGAPORE: Lee Kim 1st half net up 28 pct.</title>
<headline>Lee Kim 1st half net up 28 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(In millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			1.79    vs   1.39</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)	  2.23    vs   1.73</p>
<p>    Fully diluted basis (cents) 1.71    vs   1.73</p>
<p>    Turnover			 14.27    vs 185.06</p>
<p>    Interest expenses	     1.54    vs   0.35</p>
<p>    Pretax			    2.65    vs   2.55</p>
<p>    Tax				 1.16    vs   1.16</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (loss)     (0.50)   vs   nil</p>
<p>Note - Construction company Lee Kim Tah Holdings Ltd said the current financial year is expected to be satisfactory. It said the extraordinary item is a provision against an overseas investment in view of its current poor results.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
